{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Protect the 5 year ILR route for existing UK Ancestry visa holders",
        "additional_details": "We believe the UK Ancestry visa is more than an immigration route. It recognises the familial ties that Commonwealth citizens have with the UK through a UK-born grandparent and gives them the opportunity to build a life in their ancestral home. Moving existing visa holders onto a longer route could mean substantial extra fees that could force them to leave the UK. Their ancestral connection to this country, financial commitments, and desire to honour their British heritage deserve recognition & protection.",
        "background": "The UK Ancestry visa recognises the familial ties Commonwealth citizens have with the UK. Unlike other migration routes, it is founded on an ancestral connection to the country, so visa holders should be recognised as a distinct group and exempt from changes that would extend the settlement route.",
